# Current baseline and source delta

The original development checkout is preserved at **98bd9d913f9ddae5f0d6a3ae256bff10f25ee743**. The branch captured at implementation start is **d3d7f565c6c05ccf764fe0780fde149b7dc89b95**, in [the separate review worktree](../../AI4Research-Development/jiuwenswarm-m1-review-d3d7f56). Both remain available; no checkout files were edited. The [receipt](verification/baseline-2026-10-21.json) records changed paths and selected source hashes. A shallow-fetch update message does not establish ancestry; this review compares the exact two trees.

## What changed

The 35 changed paths concern web shell styling and inputs, reconnect/session handling, Codex device-login controls, deployment launch convenience, and M1-001/M1-006/native task records. The capsule bodies, check bundles, runner, and native adapter have no diff between these revisions. Earlier bounded CC source observations still apply to those unchanged files; they do not qualify the changed integration or a built image.

The new `deploy/m1/start-local.sh` enables an explicit loopback-only reusable bootstrap option (`AI4R_REUSABLE_LOGIN=1`); default Compose behavior remains one-use unless enabled. Source refuses a reusable bootstrap for a non-loopback IP origin. Treat either actual URL as a credential. The supplied one-use instructions belong to the earlier configuration and should not be silently rewritten as a universal rule. Empty configuration supports inspection, not research readiness.

Codex login now propagates the device user code and tracks cancellation state. These are source observations, not independently validated authentication or deployment claims. The captured task register is r45; it still reports integrated candidate NOT_BUILT and final system evidence NOT_RUN. Later child records may contain narrower build or deployed-checkpoint observations; retain their actual scope and candidate identity.

## Authority and assurance

[[Designs/Project Authority]] explains stale AGENTS and branch-local PRD/task pointers. Actual `docs/code/Missions/M1/TASKS.md` is populated; do not allocate duplicate tasks from stale registration-pending text or the older design checkout. Preserve task/IF/AC identities and reconcile source baseline receipts.

| Evidence level | Assessment |
|---|---|
| Designed | PRD and maintained design present; source-specific authority requires receipts |
| Implemented | Actual capsule, native adapter, host checks, broker, science and web code present |
| Runnable | Deployment paths exist; actual M1 build/account/resource qualification not performed here |
| Verified | Notebook tests and separate lab receipts only; neither implies M1 acceptance |
| Accepted | No new integrated M1 acceptance or CC accuracy gain established |

## Host observation

On this continuation Docker Desktop responds with Linux server 29.8.0, x86_64, 16 CPUs and approximately 8 GB daemon memory. Ubuntu-24.04 resolves the Windows Docker CLI through WSL. This supersedes the earlier unavailable-daemon observation; it does not establish a native Ubuntu daemon or GB10 support. Real lab smoke checks belong in [[Designs/Lab Progression]]. A small lab container is not an M1 production runtime.
